# Flutter/Dart coding style

Narrows `core-common-rules`' style rules to Effective Dart (Dart 3.x, sound null safety) and Flutter widget idiom.

## Naming and structure

- A widget file is named after the widget it defines (`order_summary_card.dart`
  for `OrderSummaryCard`), one primary public widget per file, matching how the
  project already splits `lib/`.
- `build()` is layout only; data fetching, formatting and validation live in a
  controller/view-model/state object the widget reads from.

## Const constructors and rebuild cost

- Mark every widget constructor `const` when all fields can be `final` and
  const-constructible.
- Use `const` at call sites too (`const SizedBox(height: 8)`); do not disable
  `prefer_const_constructors` to avoid fixing them.
- A widget with a non-const field that need not vary per build (a callback closure
  built each `build()`) hoists it out (a `static` handler, a field on the `State`)
  so the widget can be const.

## Sound null safety idiom

- Prefer `?.`/`??`/`??=` over `!`; use `!` only when non-nullability is guaranteed
  by code the analyzer cannot see (checked just above with no intervening `await`,
  or a documented invariant), with a comment when not obvious.
- Never use `!` on a value that crossed an `await` since it was last checked, or on
  a field of a widget/state that could have been disposed; re-check
  (`if (value == null) return;` or `context.mounted`) after the async gap.
- Declare a field `late` only when it is always initialized before first read
  (e.g. in `initState`).
- Give a nullable parameter a default via `??` at the point of use rather than
  threading a null check through every consumer.

## Composition over deep nesting

- Extract a widget into its own class (or a private `_SectionWidget` below the
  main widget) once a `build()` method's nesting is hard to scan.
- Flatten with `SizedBox`/`Padding` siblings and extracted widgets rather than
  nesting `Padding(child: Container(child: Column(...)))` for a visual effect a
  flatter tree gives.
- A `build()` that branches on more than two or three conditions extracts each
  branch into its own widget.

## Formatting and imports

- Format with `dart format`; do not hand-format around a configured formatter.
- Order imports `dart:` / `package:flutter` / other `package:` / relative, a blank
  line between groups, matching the project's `analysis_options.yaml`
  (`directives_ordering`).
- Relative imports within the same package's `lib/` tree, `package:` imports for
  anything outside it, matching the project's convention.
